The same seed can play out very differently in Slay the Spire 2. That amazing seed you shared with a friend turns into a nightmare for them. A brutal seed ends your win streak, but feels easy when you replay it to see what went wrong...

Try Seedline.

With over 200 hours of design and refinement, Seedline brings same-seed runs closer together while leaving vanilla probabilities almost unchanged.

Sharing seeds with friends means sharing more of the highs and lows. Replaying a tough seed becomes more useful for learning. Same-seed races between skilled players become fairer.

A simple example: reshuffling an extra time in one fight no longer changes the next fight's opening hand by itself.

The algorithms behind it are complex, but you don't need to understand them. With Seedline enabled, playing feels just like vanilla. Whether you're building a win streak or hunting for a great seed, just enjoy the added consistency.

[b]Requirements[/b]

[list]
[*]Windows and StS2 v0.113.1 on public-beta.
[*]Standard and Dread single-player runs only. Multiplayer, Blitz and custom modifiers are unsupported.
[*]Supports most commonly used mods, including modded characters, but is incompatible with Combat Solver.
[/list]

[b]Q&A[/b]

[b]Does this guarantee identical outcomes?[/b]
If all major decisions stay the same, yes! The catch is that Slay the Spire 2 has a lot of major decisions. So expect less divergence between same-seed runs, not a guarantee that they will never diverge.

[b]Does it change vanilla probabilities?[/b]
Yes. For example, we fully preserve vanilla Rare-card probabilities, but keeping card rewards consistent requires normal fights and elites to have the same Uncommon-card rates. This means elite rewards offer about 0.15 fewer Uncommon cards on average than in vanilla, while the overall Uncommon-card rate stays roughly the same. This is the mod's largest probability adjustment, but it is still small compared with the roughly 1.1 Uncommon cards you can expect to see in a single normal-fight reward.

[b]Can I use save/load to try different actions?[/b]
Yes, but save/load gives you far fewer ways to manipulate outcomes. This is a tradeoff for consistency: the actions that let you reroll results through save/load can also make same-seed runs diverge when you play without reloading. Better support for vanilla-style save/load play is planned.

[b]Do I need everything unlocked?[/b]
No. Seedline automatically uses fully unlocked content without changing your profile's unlock progress.

[b]Are other mods required?[/b]
No. Seedline also supports commonly used mods such as RitsuLib, BaseLib and Quick SL.

[b]Does it work with modded characters?[/b]
Most out-of-combat effects are supported, but most in-combat randomness, including shuffles, still follows the original rules.

[b]Can I enable or disable Seedline mid-run?[/b]
No. Seedline and vanilla run saves are not interchangeable. Start a new run after incompatible updates.

[b]Where can I report a problem?[/b]
Leave a comment on this page or join QQ group 609823795. Include versions, enabled mods, and relevant logs or screenshots.

[b]What's planned next?[/b]
Support for vanilla-style save/load play, broader mod compatibility, designs for Blitz and multiplayer modes, and write-ups explaining how Seedline works.
